isar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se distribuyen uniformemente entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 127 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 42.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.4 to 3.7. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 6. Contract [1], for 14,964 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows a pattern of contracts just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be close to the limit due to market conditions or budget constraints. The statistical ratio alone doesn't indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the dates. Look at awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same needs. Review the distribution of contracts across months to identify any unusual patterns.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["GoClxuZGTUCIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D","7OdLkmadA187u6%2B%2FR7DUoA%3D%3D","2lYAbVREQuO2gkLQ8TeYKA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}